@base = http://localhost:8080
@a = 00000000-0000-7000-8002-000000000001
@b = 00000000-0000-7000-8002-000000000002
@cus = 00000000-0000-7000-8001-000000000001

### Balance A
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{a}}/balance

### Balance B
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{b}}/balance

### Transfer £5 A → B (fresh key each run)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
X-Customer-Id: {{cus}}

{"from_account_id": "{{a}}", "to_account_id": "{{b}}", "amount_minor": 500, "currency": "GBP"}

### Transfer with a fixed key (run twice: 201, then 200 replay)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-fixed-1
X-Customer-Id: {{cus}}

{"from_account_id": "{{a}}", "to_account_id": "{{b}}", "amount_minor": 500, "currency": "GBP"}

### Same key, different amount (409)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-fixed-1
X-Customer-Id: {{cus}}

{"from_account_id": "{{a}}", "to_account_id": "{{b}}", "amount_minor": 600, "currency": "GBP"}

### Overdraft (422)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
X-Customer-Id: {{cus}}

{"from_account_id": "{{a}}", "to_account_id": "{{b}}", "amount_minor": 99999999, "currency": "GBP"}